            "review_title": "Review at Picante Latino- Gusto Latino Gourmet",
            "review_text": "Omnivore17\nNha Trang, Vietnam15 contributions\n1\nHeaven in Hanoi\nMay 2018 • Solo\nThere's fuel, and then there's food. Vietnam is one big fuel dump. This restaurant serves great food. I was kind of dying of starvation in Tay Ho and then I discovered Picante. Perfect dinner: finely nuanced, perfectly seasoned, excellent presentation. I recommend this restaurant above all others in Vietnam - how's that for a recommendation? I had the fish ceviche which was very spicy more like a Thai dish, and the steak with chimichurri sauce. Every morsel was authentic and delicious. If all you're looking for is a hamburger fix or a bowl of noodles for under a dollar, this is not your home away from home. But for those world travelers who demand and appreciate three star food, this is your new home. It seems to have an excellent wine menu as well.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten May 20, 2018",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-15",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
